\section{Smart Compress Evaluation Across Task Suites}
\label{app:cross_suite}

Table~\ref{tab:cross_suite} reports the performance of Smart Compress ($M{=}32$) across three LIBERO suites. All suites are in-distribution: the training set (HuggingFaceVLA/libero) covers Object, Spatial, Goal, and Long (40 tasks, 1693 episodes total). On LIBERO-Goal, performance drops from 63.0\% to 56.4\% ($-6.6$pp). On LIBERO-Spatial, Smart Compress achieves 53.2\% SR, where the official SmolVLA checkpoint scores 43.8\% and hard pruning yields 0\%. While 53.2\% nominally exceeds the official Spatial baseline, this difference concentrates in two of ten tasks (+44pp and +48pp respectively); the remaining eight tasks show a net difference of only +0.2pp. We therefore do not treat the Spatial comparison as evidence that re-encoding improves over the uncompressed official baseline. The qualitative conclusion holds regardless: the cliff-edge pattern and re-encoding recovery generalize across task structures within the training distribution. The LIBERO-Goal decline indicates that re-encoding benefits vary across task structures.

